@joperezr 
I forgot to mention: currently, I am using `string searchBase = "DC=inc,DC=company,DC=com";` This fails on Linux but works on Windows (with the setup described above). 
However, If I instead use `string searchBase = "CN=Users,DC=inc,DC=company,DC=com";` I get the users in the "Users" path (missing users that are in the top level DC=inc,DC=company,DC=com that were returned on Windows using the first `searchBase`. Hopefully that info helps narrow down the discrepancy.

Based on @makrattaur's analysis, there are two problems here: `SessionOptions.ReferralChasing` is ineffective, and we can't set rebind callbacks in Linux.

I have a commit to be able to make the `ReferralChasing` property effective, which should "resolve" this particular problem. If accepted, we should open a separate issue to track setting rebind callbacks.

@danmoseley, can you assign this to me, and add the `os-linux` label? We might want to rename this issue too, if it's ok with OP.
